{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Science or Science Fiction?"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Everyday Objects "}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le04ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Real Conditional: Talking About The Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the Real conditional with If clauses to talk about future situations and outcomes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you're going to move into the future with your home appliances, soon you'll have a lot of ultramodern gadgets to choose from. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Real Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will, or will not happen. <br> The parts of the sentence are divided into two clauses: the <span class=\"italic\"> If</span> clause and  the <span class=\"italic\">Condition </span>clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple/Present continuous \u2026 will/Present Continuous / be going to</span>  <br>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> We'll need a holographic TV is we're going to keep up.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use an Imperative verb in the main clause if you are making offers, giving instructions, or suggesting advice.   <br>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> Get one of these if you want to save water.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you wait for that new stove, you'll be able to change the way you cook all together soon with heatless cooking. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you are wondering what it is, you'll be finding out right here."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you cook on an induction cooktop, only the pan and food contained within it become hot."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Choose an induction stove if you want the heat to be generated on the pan rather than from the stove."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verbs Followed by -ing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about two actions linked together, you normally use two verbs. The first verb follows the rules of conjugation for the sentence, while the second verb can be a verb in the -ing form."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't mind waiting for new innovations, do you?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use two verbs to talk about two connected actions. The main verb introduces the main action, and the second verb in the -ing form gives more information about that action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some verbs followed by -ing are <span class=\"italic\">imagine, enjoy, consider, mind, keep, love/hate </span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Subject + first verb + -ing form of the second verb</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at some examples from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Stores in the U.S. are anticipating getting his technology soon."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Consider cooking where the heat is generated by electromagnetic currents in the burners that respond to metal cooking pots and pans."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Imagine removing a pan from from the burner and the cooktop surface becomes almost cool to the touch."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A new company is proposing finding ways to refresh holographic images faster. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "With this you will enjoy seeing things move and look  as they should. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Keep looking for them at a store near you!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ultramodern "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "incorporating ideas, styles, or techniques only recently developed or available"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you're going to move into the future with your home appliances, soon you'll have a lot of ultramodern gadgets to choose from."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about appliances of the future."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "innovation "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a new idea or method"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't mind waiting for new innovations, do you?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to anticipate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to imagine or expect something to happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Stores in the U.S. are anticipating getting his technology soon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heatless "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without generating heat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you wait for that new stove, you'll be able to change the way you cook all together soon with heatless cooking. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "electromagnetic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "of or relating to the interrelation of electric currents or fields and magnetic fields"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Consider cooking where the heat is generated by electromagnetic currents in the burners that respond to metal cooking pots and pans."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "induction "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "heating and object without electricity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you cook on an induction cooktop, only the pan and food contained within it become hot. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "burner "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "part of stove which produces heat for cooking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Imagine removing a pan from  the burner and the cooktop surface becomes almost cool to the touch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "holographic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "projecting 3D images created by light beams"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If we're going to have holographic TVs for the consumer market, the new, quick refresh rates will have to work and keep working. Keep looking for them at a store near you!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "waterless "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without the use of water"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are also recommending waiting for the hero of the century, the waterless washing machine."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "absorbent "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "able to take in liquids"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:These beads are more absorbent than water, allowing them to absorb stains right into their core."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le04ob01aud10"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Decide on a new appliance that people will want to use."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sketch out a basic drawing or use a picture that's of something similar and annotate it with the innovations and how they are used."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about using this item in the future with \u2018if'."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your appliance to a partner or group."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to other presentations"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the advantages of such items together."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I decide on a new appliance that people will want to use."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I annotate an image of the item."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the item using real conditionals and verbs followed by gerunds."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss items with a partner or group."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment