company is proposing finding ways to refresh holographic images faster. With this you will enjoy seeing things move and look  as they should. If we're going to have holographic TVs for the consumer market, the new, quick refresh rates will have to work and keep working. Keep looking for them at a store near you!<br/><br/>We are also recommending waiting for the hero of the century, the waterless washing machine. Get one of these if you want to save on water! Xeros reports their machines  using 90% less water than other conventional machines. If you're going to do that, you need to clean using their nylon polymer beads. These beads are more absorbent than water, allowing them to absorb stains right into their core.", "id": 3, "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn11le04ob01re2vid01"}}], "id": 2, "template_override": 1, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": []}]}]}